Package: retestR
Title: Model-Based Anomaly Detection for Repeat Test-Takers
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Daniel", "Edi", email = "danieledi2026@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5475-819X"))
Description: Flags repeat test-takers whose second-attempt performance departs
    from what a growth model predicts, using independent evidence sources:
    model-expected score gain (accounting for regression to the mean, time
    between attempts and remediation), differential performance on exposed
    versus new items, and differential response speed. Evidence is combined
    into a risk index calibrated by parametric bootstrap under the
    no-misconduct model, so flagging thresholds carry explicit false-positive
    rates.
